==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*2 [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 2~8 seconds<sup>60f~240f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**35 [[The Thrillerz|Thrillerz]] spawn, delay 1.67~3.33 seconds<sup>50f~100f</sup>.
**3 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**3 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Le'noir]] spawns.
**8 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Most of the enemies here are just peons designed to get in your way, except for Dark Otter and Le'noir. Simply spamming [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] will clear out the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] and the occasional Sir Rel.

For the Dark Otter, bring [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bomber Cat]] along with [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or just any [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark attacker]], they will also help with Le'noir.

[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] can OHKO the Zombie peons due to their low magnifications, which can clear the way for Bombercat, and any other attackers.

